# Percentage addition with the percentage on the left rejected

Verifies a percentage on the left of addition has no reference magnitude and is rejected at compile time. An unannotated 50% literal carries the percentage subtype with no relative rule for a plain right operand, so the compiler reports the undefined operand pair instead of guessing a fraction base.

>>> source
print(50% + 100)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: operator `+` is not defined for `int64[%]` and `int64` at Span { start: 6, end: 15 }

<<< exit
1
